# Fix for the WSL2 default-memory gotcha (PLAN.md §9 risk register): Docker
# Desktop's WSL2 backend caps the VM at 50% of host RAM by default, which on
# a 16 GB box (8 GB) is not enough headroom for vLLM to load an ~8.5 GB
# model plus its own overhead — it will OOM at startup.
#
# Only needed if the GPU box runs Windows + Docker Desktop; skip entirely on
# native Linux.
#
# 1. Copy this file to C:\Users\<you>\.wslconfig  (on Windows, NOT inside WSL)
# 2. From PowerShell: wsl --shutdown
# 3. Restart Docker Desktop

[wsl2]
memory=12GB
swap=4GB
